  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "School of Argentine concert composers, from the late nineteenth to the mid-twentieth century, who built art music on criollo and gaucho folk sources: Alberto Williams, founder of the Buenos Aires Conservatory, Julián Aguirre, Carlos López Buchardo and Luis Gianneo, then Alberto Ginastera, whose ballet Estancia ends in a malambo, with Carlos Guastavino continuing the idiom in songs and piano pieces. They set the rhythms and modal turns of the malambo, gato, zamba, huella and vidala in orchestral, piano and vocal writing.",
